Licensing note (dual-licensing history)
========================================
pyGuidos was originally released under the European Union Public Licence
(EUPL-1.2). Starting with version 2.6.0, which incorporated the
GPLv3-licensed miallib MSPA engine, the project is distributed under the GNU
General Public License v3 or later. Version 2.6.1 replaces the vendored
miallib C sources with a native-Python re-implementation of the same MSPA
algorithm (`pyguidos/engine_mspa.py`). This Python module is a derivative
work of the GPLv3 miallib sources (it is a line-by-line port that reproduces
the original algorithm), so the GPLv3 continues to apply to the package as a
whole. The EUPL-1.2 is listed as compatible with the GPLv3.


Third-party components and attribution
=======================================

Morphological Spatial Pattern Analysis (MSPA)
---------------------------------------------
The MSPA engine in `pyguidos/engine_mspa.py` is a native-Python
re-implementation of the MSPA algorithm (`segmentBinaryPatterns`) from the
`miallib` C library (Morphological Image Analysis library), Copyright (C)
Pierre Soille and collaborators, distributed under the GNU General Public
License v3 or later. The MSPA algorithm and its GuidosToolbox implementation
are the work of Pierre Soille and Peter Vogt (European Commission, Joint
Research Centre).

Reference:
  Soille P, Vogt P (2009). Morphological segmentation of binary patterns.
  Pattern Recognition Letters 30(4):456-459.
  DOI: 10.1016/j.patrec.2008.10.015

Because `pyguidos/engine_mspa.py` is derived from these GPLv3 sources, the
pyGuidos package as a whole is distributed under the GPLv3 (see LICENSE).

The Python port reproduces the miallib result bit-for-bit on the interior of
the image across edge widths, 4- and 8-connectivity, and the transition and
internal options. The only intentional deviation is a symmetric border
treatment on the right/bottom image edges (miallib has a one-pixel
asymmetry there); see the notes in `pyguidos/engine_mspa.py`.
